{"timestamp":"2026-11-21T21:50:48.715Z","ordinal":35735,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20014-b98e-7f50-9b44-1c38f2a1201a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-0f92ebd5-af49-4b0a-b816-ace9e6a00665","process_id":"71701","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git grep -n -E 'WP-P10-02|P10-02|durable budget|PA-2 verified merge arbitration|Goal semantics' origin/main -- docs/v1.3.0 docs/assurance docs/v1.2.2 | head -140 && git show origin/main:cli/test/subagent_delegation_authority.test.ts && git show origin/main:cli/test/harness.test.ts | sed -n '770,930p;1080,1160p;1280,1345p' && git show origin/main:cli/test/objective_continuation.test.ts | sed -n '180,275p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git grep -n -E 'WP-P10-02|P10-02|durable budget|PA-2 verified merge arbitration|Goal semantics' origin/main -- docs/v1.3.0 docs/assurance docs/v1.2.2 | head -140 && git show origin/main:cli/test/subagent_delegation_authority.test.ts && git show origin/main:cli/test/harness.test.ts | sed -n '770,930p;1080,1160p;1280,1345p' && git show origin/main:cli/test/objective_continuation.test.ts | sed -n '180,275p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"origin/main:docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:33:## WP-P10-02 — Durable task-level execution budgets\norigin/main:docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:79:**Priority:** P1 · **Complexity:** M/L · **Dependencies:** WP-P10-02.\norigin/main:docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:108:2. **WP-P10-02** aggregate budgets across direct, delegated, retry and resume paths (P0).\norigin/main:docs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:19:- v1.3 PA-1, PA-2 and PA-3 already cover parallel visibility, verified integration and goal semantics. PA-4 stages this assignment against those units and the active WP-P10-02 durable-budget work.\norigin/main:docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:96:| PA-3 | Goal semantics: a ledger entry active from an earlier process resumes **paused** (opencode `goal.ts` boot id), stall counting by failure fingerprint and not turn count, completion decided only by a verifier receipt, an optional token budget rolling up from sub-operations (reference: Codex goal budget); `/team` leaves experimental only after PA-1 and PA-2 | stale goal resumes paused with a visible reason; a model \"I am done\" does not complete a goal | M | P2 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:97:| PA-4 | **Bounded delegation and workflow commands** (trail 428; [baseline](PA4_BASELINE.md)): extend transient `spawn_subagent` and durable operations with a shared validated delegation contract/outcome, enforce authority intersection and recursive/resource limits, then expose real `/goal`, `/loop`, and `/batch` lifecycles through REPL and TUI/sidecar. Reuse `TeamOrchestrator`, `ConvergenceScheduler`, `OperationStore`, `ResourceRegistry`, specialist profiles, provider recovery, completion evidence, and existing stagnation detectors; do not add a second scheduler or workflow store. `/goal` owns an immutable objective and requirement/evidence ledger; `/loop` is bounded and verifier-driven; `/batch` validates a task graph and maps it into existing work units. Parsing, cancellation, pause/resume, status, recovery, and provider-neutral fixtures are part of each command contract. Spec-format validation may proceed independently; lifecycle and shared-contract work depends on PA-1/PA-2 evidence and WP-P10-02, with `/goal` semantics aligned to PA-3. | prompt-only subagent compatibility; parent/profile/session authority intersection and enforced recursive limits; typed non-success and unknown-effect outcomes; each command has durable state, lifecycle controls, recovery and status through supported interfaces; dependency and workspace conflicts cannot silently complete or overwrite; deterministic verifiers and independent review gate acceptance; standard-contract mock plus existing local/cloud fixtures pass without provider changes | L (staged packages) | P1 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:105:PA-4 is staged: the existing operation-spec validator can be reused independently; command lifecycles and shared delegation changes follow WP-P10-02 and verified PA-1/PA-2 gates. `/goal` must also satisfy PA-3 before promotion.\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport test from \"node:test\";\nimport { dispatchToolCallImpl } from \"../src/core/dispatch_tool_call.js\";\nimport { resolveDelegationContract } from \"../src/core/delegation_contract.js\";\n\ntest(\"delegation contract refuses capabilities outside the inherited intersection\", () => {\n  const contract = {\n    id: \"child-1\",\n    parentId: \"parent-1\",\n    objective: \"Inspect source\",\n    profile: \"semantic_explorer\",\n    inputs: {},\n    authorizedScope: [\"src\"],\n    permittedCapabilities: [\"fs_read\"],\n    executionMode: \"transient\" as const,\n    requiresVerification: false,\n    requiresIndependentReview: false,\n  };\n  const layers = [\"parent\", \"profile\", \"task\", \"session\", \"workspace\"].map((source) => ({\n    source: source as \"parent\" | \"profile\" | \"task\" | \"session\" | \"workspace\",\n    authorizedScope: [\"*\"],\n    permittedCapabilities: [\"fs_read\"],\n  }));\n  assert.deepEqual(resolveDelegationContract(contract, layers).permittedCapabilities, [\"fs_read\"]);\n  assert.throws(() => resolveDelegationContract({ ...contract, permittedCapabilities: [\"fs_write\"] }, layers), /unauthorized capability/);\n});\n\ntest(\"dispatcher denies a delegated tool omitted from its host allowlist\", async () => {\n  const agent: any = {\n    delegatedToolAllowList: new Set([\"read_file\"]),\n    config: { dryRun: false },\n    activeWorktree: undefined,\n    currentTaskId: \"parent-1\",\n    capabilityRegistry: { getByToolName: (name: string) => ({ id: name }) },\n    lastToolReceipts: [],\n    getEffectiveTools: () => [],\n  };\n  const result = await dispatchToolCallImpl.call(agent, {\n    id: \"call-1\",\n    function: { name: \"write_file\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ path: \"src/a.ts\", content: \"bad\" }) },\n  } as any, 1, \"subagent\");\n  assert.equal(result.receipt.status, \"DENIED\");\n  assert.equal(result.receipt.denialReason, \"DELEGATION_AUTHORITY\");\n  assert.equal(result.receipt.candidateMutated, false);\n});\n    try {\n      const port = await new Promise<number>((resolve) => server.listen(0, \"127.0.0.1\", () => resolve((server.address() as any).port)));\n      agent = new AutonomousAgent({ endpoint: `http://127.0.0.1:${port}/v1`, model: \"test\", maxSteps: 2, temperature: 0, workspace: repo, shell: \"bash\", worktree: true, approvalMode: \"auto\", fullAccess: true });\n      await agent.run(\"do not merge an unverified change\");\n      const active = agent.getActiveWorktree();\n      assert.ok(active, \"missing verification retains the speculative worktree\");\n      assert.strictEqual((agent as any).verifiedWorktreeCompletion, false);\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(active!.worktreePath, \"unverified.txt\")), true);\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(repo, \"unverified.txt\")), false);\n      assert.strictEqual(agent.discardActiveWorktree().success, true);\n      // With no applicable verifier, task_completed is accepted as UNVERIFIED (no guessed `npm test` refusal loop),\n      // so the model is not asked for a second turn.\n      assert.strictEqual(requests, 1);\n      const turn = agent.getLastTurnResult();\n      assert.strictEqual(turn?.execution, \"COMPLETED\");\n      assert.strictEqual(turn?.outcome, \"UNVERIFIED\");\n      assert.strictEqual(turn?.reason, \"NO_APPLICABLE_VERIFIER\");\n    } finally {\n      if (agent?.getActiveWorktree()) agent.discardActiveWorktree();\n      agent?.shutdown();\n      server.closeAllConnections();\n      await new Promise<void>((resolve) => server.close(() => resolve()));\n      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"issue 11 worktree subagents cannot mutate the original workspace\", async () => {\n    const repo = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-subagent-authority-\"));\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(repo, \"base.txt\"), \"base\\n\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(repo, \"Makefile\"), \"test:\\n\\t@true\\n\");\n    execSync(\"git init -q && git config user.name 'Nexus Test' && git config user.email 'nexus@example.invalid' && git add . && git commit -qm baseline\", { cwd: repo, stdio: \"ignore\" });\n    const originalWorkspaceWrite = path.join(repo, \"subagent-root-escape.txt\");\n    let streamRequests = 0;\n    let childRequests = 0;\n    const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {\n      if (req.headers[\"x-nexus-purpose\"] === \"capabilities\") { res.setHeader(\"content-type\", \"application/json\"); res.end('{\"data\":[]}'); return; } // capability discovery: no catalog\n      let body = \"\";\n      req.on(\"data\", (chunk) => { body += chunk; });\n      req.on(\"end\", () => {\n        const request = JSON.parse(body || \"{}\");\n        if (request.stream) {\n          streamRequests++;\n          const calls = streamRequests === 1 ? [\n            { index: 0, id: \"write\", type: \"function\", function: { name: \"write_file\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ path: \"parent-worktree.txt\", content: \"parent\\n\" }) } },\n            { index: 1, id: \"spawn\", type: \"function\", function: { name: \"spawn_subagent\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ prompt: \"write to the original checkout\", profile: \"implementer\", max_steps: 3 }) } },\n            { index: 2, id: \"complete\", type: \"function\", function: { name: \"task_completed\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ summary: \"Parent task finished.\" }) } },\n          ] : [];\n          res.writeHead(200, { \"Content-Type\": \"text/event-stream\" });\n          res.end(`data: ${JSON.stringify({ choices: [{ delta: { content: \"Exercise inherited worktree authority.\", tool_calls: calls } }] })}\\n\\ndata: [DONE]\\n\\n`);\n          return;\n        }\n        childRequests++;\n        if (childRequests === 3) {\n          res.writeHead(200, { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" });\n          res.end(JSON.stringify({ choices: [{ message: { role: \"assistant\", content: \"The attempted write escaped the authorized worktree, so I stopped and reported the boundary failure.\" } }] }));\n          return;\n        }\n        const call = childRequests === 1\n          ? { name: \"run_command\", args: { command: \"printf child > child-worktree.txt\" } }\n          : { name: \"run_command\", args: { command: `printf escaped > ${JSON.stringify(originalWorkspaceWrite)}` } };\n        res.writeHead(200, { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" });\n        res.end(JSON.stringify({ choices: [{ message: { role: \"assistant\", tool_calls: [{ id: `child-${childRequests}`, type: \"function\", function: { name: call.name, arguments: JSON.stringify(call.args) } }] } }] }));\n      });\n    });\n    let agent: AutonomousAgent | undefined;\n    try {\n      const port = await new Promise<number>((resolve) => server.listen(0, \"127.0.0.1\", () => resolve((server.address() as any).port)));\n      // The parent spends one task-wide inference step before delegating; leave three for the child sequence.\n      agent = new AutonomousAgent({ endpoint: `http://127.0.0.1:${port}/v1`, model: \"test\", maxSteps: 4, temperature: 0, workspace: repo, shell: \"bash\", worktree: true, approvalMode: \"auto\", fullAccess: true });\n      await agent.run(\"exercise child mutation boundary\");\n      const active = agent.getActiveWorktree();\n      assert.ok(active, \"unverified parent worktree remains recoverable\");\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(originalWorkspaceWrite), false, \"child shell must not mutate the original checkout\");\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(active!.worktreePath, \"parent-worktree.txt\")), true, \"parent mutation remains in its intended worktree\");\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(active!.worktreePath, \"child-worktree.txt\")), true, \"child retains the parent's authorized mutation destination\");\n      assert.strictEqual(streamRequests, 1);\n      assert.strictEqual(childRequests, 3);\n      assert.strictEqual(agent.discardActiveWorktree().success, true);\n    } finally {\n      agent?.shutdown();\n      server.closeAllConnections();\n      await new Promise<void>((resolve) => server.close(() => resolve()));\n      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"worktree-enabled runSubagent refuses to start without inherited worktree authority\", async () => {\n    const repo = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-subagent-no-authority-\"));\n    execSync(\"git init -q\", { cwd: repo, stdio: \"ignore\" });\n    let requests = 0;\n    const server = http.createServer((req, res) => { if (req.headers[\"x-nexus-purpose\"] === \"capabilities\") { res.end('{\"data\":[]}'); return; } requests++; res.writeHead(500).end(); });\n    let agent: AutonomousAgent | undefined;\n    try {\n      const port = await new Promise<number>((resolve) => server.listen(0, \"127.0.0.1\", () => resolve((server.address() as any).port)));\n      agent = new AutonomousAgent({ endpoint: `http://127.0.0.1:${port}/v1`, model: \"test\", maxSteps: 2, temperature: 0, workspace: repo, shell: \"bash\", worktree: true });\n      await assert.rejects(agent.runSubagent(\"must not dispatch without a worktree\"), /without an established worktree authority/);\n      assert.strictEqual(requests, 0, \"refusal happens before inference\");\n      assert.strictEqual(execSync(\"git status --porcelain\", { cwd: repo, encoding: \"utf8\" }), \"\");\n    } finally {\n      agent?.shutdown();\n      server.closeAllConnections();\n      await new Promise<void>((resolve) => server.close(() => resolve()));\n      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"spawned worktree subagent preserves parent read-only authority\", async () => {\n    const repo = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-subagent-readonly-\"));\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(repo, \"base.txt\"), \"base\\n\");\n    execSync(\"git init -q && git config user.name 'Nexus Test' && git config user.email 'nexus@example.invalid' && git add . && git commit -qm baseline\", { cwd: repo, stdio: \"ignore\" });\n    let streamRequests = 0;\n    let childRequests = 0;\n    let childDeniedWrite = false;\n    const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {\n      if (req.headers[\"x-nexus-purpose\"] === \"capabilities\") { res.setHeader(\"content-type\", \"application/json\"); res.end('{\"data\":[]}'); return; } // capability discovery: no catalog\n      let body = \"\";\n      req.on(\"data\", (chunk) => { body += chunk; });\n      req.on(\"end\", () => {\n        const request = JSON.parse(body || \"{}\");\n        if (request.stream) {\n          streamRequests++;\n          const calls = streamRequests === 1 ? [\n            { index: 0, id: \"spawn\", type: \"function\", function: { name: \"spawn_subagent\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ prompt: \"attempt a prohibited write\", max_steps: 2 }) } },\n            { index: 1, id: \"complete\", type: \"function\", function: { name: \"task_completed\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ summary: \"Read-only task complete.\" }) } },\n          ] : [];\n          res.writeHead(200, { \"Content-Type\": \"text/event-stream\" });\n          res.end(`data: ${JSON.stringify({ choices: [{ delta: { content: \"Respect read-only authority.\", tool_calls: calls } }] })}\\n\\ndata: [DONE]\\n\\n`);\n          return;\n        }\n        childRequests++;\n        if (childRequests > 1) {\n          const toolMessage = (request.messages || []).find((message: any) => message.role === \"tool\");\n          childDeniedWrite = /Read-only mode violation|Delegation authority denied|not permitted for role/.test(String(toolMessage?.content || \"\"));\n        }\n        const call = childRequests === 1\n          ? { name: \"write_file\", args: { path: \"read-only-child.txt\", content: \"must not write\" } }\n          : { name: \"task_completed\", args: { summary: \"Child finished.\" } };\n        res.writeHead(200, { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" });\n        res.end(JSON.stringify({ choices: [{ message: { role: \"assistant\", tool_calls: [{ id: `child-${childRequests}`, type: \"function\", function: { name: call.name, arguments: JSON.stringify(call.args) } }] } }] }));\n      });\n    });\n    let agent: AutonomousAgent | undefined;\n    try {\n      const port = await new Promise<number>((resolve) => server.listen(0, \"127.0.0.1\", () => resolve((server.address() as any).port)));\n      // The parent's delegation request consumes one step; reserve two more for the child's refusal and report.\n      agent = new AutonomousAgent({ endpoint: `http://127.0.0.1:${port}/v1`, model: \"test\", maxSteps: 3, temperature: 0, workspace: repo, shell: \"bash\", worktree: true, readOnly: true });\n      await agent.run(\"keep subagent read-only\");\n      assert.strictEqual(childRequests, 2);\n      assert.strictEqual(childDeniedWrite, true, \"the child must receive the parent read-only tool policy\");\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(repo, \"read-only-child.txt\")), false);\n      assert.strictEqual(agent.getActiveWorktree(), undefined, \"no-change read-only task resolves without a mutation merge\");\n    } finally {\n      if (agent?.getActiveWorktree()) agent.discardActiveWorktree();\n      agent?.shutdown();\n      server.closeAllConnections();\n      await new Promise<void>((resolve) => server.close(() => resolve()));\n      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"discovered verification success does not authorize worktree merge\", async () => {\n        content: \"Hello Dry Run!\",\n      });\n      assert.strictEqual(resWrite.success, true);\n      const parsedWrite = JSON.parse(resWrite.output);\n      assert.strictEqual(parsedWrite.dry_run, true);\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(tmpDir, \"simulated.txt\")), false);\n\n      // 2. mutating command simulation\n      const resCmd = await bridge.executeTool(\"run_command\", {\n        command: \"touch dummy_file.txt\",\n      });\n      assert.strictEqual(resCmd.success, true);\n      assert.ok(resCmd.output.includes(\"DRY-RUN SIMULATION\"));\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(tmpDir, \"dummy_file.txt\")), false);\n\n      // 3. safe command allowed in dry-run\n      const resSafe = await bridge.executeTool(\"run_command\", {\n        command: \"echo 'safe probe'\",\n      });\n      assert.strictEqual(resSafe.success, true);\n      assert.ok(resSafe.output.includes(\"safe probe\"));\n    } finally {\n      bridge.shutdown();\n      fs.rmSync(tmpDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"RustCoreBridge read-only mode blocks file edits and non-safe commands\", async () => {\n    const tmpDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus_readonly_test_\"));\n    const { RustCoreBridge } = await import(\"../src/tools.js\");\n    const bridge = new RustCoreBridge(tmpDir, \"bash\", undefined, false, true);\n    try {\n      const resWrite = await bridge.executeTool(\"write_file\", {\n        path: \"blocked.txt\",\n        content: \"Should fail\",\n      });\n      assert.strictEqual(resWrite.success, false);\n      assert.ok(resWrite.error?.includes(\"Read-only mode violation\"));\n\n      const resCmd = await bridge.executeTool(\"run_command\", {\n        command: \"rm -f something.txt\",\n      });\n      assert.strictEqual(resCmd.success, false);\n      assert.ok(resCmd.error?.includes(\"Read-only mode violation\"));\n\n      const mutatedPaths: string[] = [];\n      for (const [command, target] of [\n        [\"echo payload > echo-redirection.txt\", \"echo-redirection.txt\"],\n        [\"ls .; echo payload > compound-redirection.txt\", \"compound-redirection.txt\"],\n        [\"cat /etc/hosts > cat-redirection.txt\", \"cat-redirection.txt\"],\n        [\"echo payload | tee tee-redirection.txt\", \"tee-redirection.txt\"],\n        [\"git status && echo payload > chained-redirection.txt\", \"chained-redirection.txt\"],\n      ]) {\n        await bridge.executeTool(\"run_command\", { command });\n        if (fs.existsSync(path.join(tmpDir, target))) mutatedPaths.push(target);\n      }\n      assert.deepStrictEqual(mutatedPaths, [], \"read-only shell cannot mutate through redirection or compound syntax\");\n    } finally {\n      bridge.shutdown();\n      fs.rmSync(tmpDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"RustCoreBridge fails closed when an isolated worktree shell loses its sandbox\", async () => {\n    const tmpDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus_required_sandbox_\"));\n    const { RustCoreBridge } = await import(\"../src/tools.js\");\n    const bridge = new RustCoreBridge(tmpDir, \"bash\", undefined, false, false, \"none\", true);\n    try {\n      const result = await bridge.executeTool(\"run_command\", { command: \"echo escaped > fallback-mutation.txt\" });\n      assert.strictEqual(result.success, false);\n      assert.ok(result.error?.includes(\"Worktree isolation violation\"));\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(tmpDir, \"fallback-mutation.txt\")), false);\n    } finally {\n      bridge.shutdown();\n      fs.rmSync(tmpDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"run_tests keeps repository test side effects inside worktree authority and honors read-only, dry-run, and required sandbox\", async () => {\n    const base = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-run-tests-authority-\"));\n    const repo = path.join(base, \"repo\");\n    } finally {\n      unavailableSandbox.shutdown();\n      noSandbox.shutdown();\n      process.env.PATH = oldPath;\n      fs.rmSync(base, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"read-only subagent run_tests cannot mutate the parent worktree, original repository, or outside path\", async () => {\n    const base = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-subagent-run-tests-authority-\"));\n    const repo = path.join(base, \"repo\");\n    fs.mkdirSync(repo);\n    const rootTarget = path.join(repo, \"test-wrote-root.txt\");\n    const outsideTarget = path.join(base, \"test-wrote-outside.txt\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(repo, \"Makefile\"), [\n      \"test:\",\n      `\\t@mkdir -p generated; printf worktree > generated/test-output.txt 2>/dev/null; printf root > ${JSON.stringify(rootTarget)} 2>/dev/null; printf outside > ${JSON.stringify(outsideTarget)} 2>/dev/null; true`,\n      \"\",\n    ].join(\"\\n\"));\n    execSync(\"git init -q && git config user.name 'Nexus Test' && git config user.email 'nexus@example.invalid' && git add . && git commit -qm baseline\", { cwd: repo, stdio: \"ignore\" });\n    let parentRequests = 0;\n    let childRequests = 0;\n    const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {\n      if (req.headers[\"x-nexus-purpose\"] === \"capabilities\") { res.setHeader(\"content-type\", \"application/json\"); res.end('{\"data\":[]}'); return; } // capability discovery: no catalog\n      let body = \"\";\n      req.on(\"data\", (chunk) => { body += chunk; });\n      req.on(\"end\", () => {\n        const request = JSON.parse(body || \"{}\");\n        if (request.stream) {\n          parentRequests++;\n          const calls = parentRequests === 1 ? [\n            { index: 0, id: \"spawn\", type: \"function\", function: { name: \"spawn_subagent\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ prompt: \"run the repository tests\", profile: \"tester\", max_steps: 2 }) } },\n            { index: 1, id: \"complete\", type: \"function\", function: { name: \"task_completed\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ summary: \"Parent finished.\" }) } },\n          ] : [];\n          res.writeHead(200, { \"Content-Type\": \"text/event-stream\" });\n          res.end(`data: ${JSON.stringify({ choices: [{ delta: { content: \"Delegate the test request.\", tool_calls: calls } }] })}\\n\\ndata: [DONE]\\n\\n`);\n          return;\n        }\n        childRequests++;\n        const call = childRequests === 1\n          ? { name: \"run_tests\", args: {} }\n          : { name: \"task_completed\", args: { summary: \"Child finished.\" } };\n        res.writeHead(200, { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" });\n        res.end(JSON.stringify({ choices: [{ message: { role: \"assistant\", tool_calls: [{ id: `child-${childRequests}`, type: \"function\", function: { name: call.name, arguments: JSON.stringify(call.args) } }] } }] }));\n      });\n    });\n    let agent: AutonomousAgent | undefined;\n    try {\n      const port = await new Promise<number>((resolve) => server.listen(0, \"127.0.0.1\", () => resolve((server.address() as any).port)));\n      // The parent spends one step delegating; reserve two child steps for run_tests and its completion report.\n      agent = new AutonomousAgent({ endpoint: `http://127.0.0.1:${port}/v1`, model: \"test\", maxSteps: 3, temperature: 0, workspace: repo, shell: \"bash\", worktree: true, readOnly: true });\n      await agent.run(\"delegate a read-only test request\");\n      const active = agent.getActiveWorktree();\n      assert.strictEqual(childRequests, 2, \"the subagent receives a run_tests tool result and then completes\");\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(active?.worktreePath || \"\", \"generated\", \"test-output.txt\")), false);\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(rootTarget), false, \"the subagent cannot mutate the original checkout\");\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(outsideTarget), false, \"the subagent cannot mutate outside the parent boundary\");\n      assert.strictEqual(parentRequests, 1);\n    } finally {\n      if (agent?.getActiveWorktree()) agent.discardActiveWorktree();\n      agent?.shutdown();\n      server.closeAllConnections();\n      await new Promise<void>((resolve) => server.close(() => resolve()));\n      fs.rmSync(base, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"the total step budget is shared by durable resume instead of resetting per invocation\", { timeout: 60_000 }, async () => {\n    const gw = await startGateway((n) => write(`resume-${n}.txt`));\n    const repo = makeRepo();\n    const agent = quiet(new AutonomousAgent(cfg(gw.url, repo, {\n      maxSteps: 30,\n      continuation: { ...DEFAULT_CONTINUATION, maxTotalSteps: 2 },\n    })));\n    try {\n      const first = await agent.runTurn(\"Keep writing distinct files.\");\n      assert.equal(first.reason, \"STEP_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED\");\n      assert.equal(first.steps.used, 2);\n      assert.equal(gw.requests.length, 2);\n\n      const resumed = await agent.runTurn(\"\", undefined, { resume: true });\n      assert.equal(resumed.execution, \"LIMIT_REACHED\");\n      assert.equal(resumed.reason, \"STEP_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED\");\n      assert.equal(gw.requests.length, 2, \"resume at an exhausted budget submits no new inference request\");\n    } finally {\n      agent.shutdown();\n      await gw.close();\n      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"a delegated helper consumes only the parent's remaining durable steps\", { timeout: 60_000 }, async () => {\n    let writes = 0;\n    const gw = await startGateway((_n, body) => {\n      const subagent = (body.messages as any[]).some((message) => typeof message.content === \"string\" && message.content.includes(\"[Subagent Objective]\"));\n      if (!subagent) return { kind: \"tools\", calls: [{ name: \"spawn_subagent\", args: { prompt: \"write until stopped\", profile: \"implementer\" } }] };\n      return write(`shared-${++writes}.txt`);\n    });\n    const repo = makeRepo();\n    const agent = quiet(new AutonomousAgent(cfg(gw.url, repo, {\n      worktree: true,\n      continuation: { ...DEFAULT_CONTINUATION, maxTotalSteps: 3 },\n    })));\n    try {\n      const turn = await agent.runTurn(\"Delegate an open-ended sequence of writes.\");\n      assert.equal(turn.execution, \"LIMIT_REACHED\");\n      assert.equal(turn.reason, \"STEP_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED\");\n      assert.equal(turn.steps.used, 3);\n      assert.equal(agent.getObjective()!.execution!.cumulativeSteps, 3);\n      assert.equal(gw.requests.length, 3, \"one parent request and exactly two delegated requests consumed the budget\");\n      assert.equal(writes, 2);\n      const workspace = agent.getActiveWorktree()?.worktreePath ?? repo;\n      assert.ok(fs.existsSync(path.join(workspace, \"shared-1.txt\")));\n      assert.ok(fs.existsSync(path.join(workspace, \"shared-2.txt\")));\n    } finally {\n      if (agent.getActiveWorktree()) agent.discardActiveWorktree();\n      agent.shutdown();\n      await gw.close();\n      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"a delegated inference is not sent when saving its shared budget fails\", { timeout: 60_000 }, async () => {\n    const gw = await startGateway((n) => n === 1\n      ? { kind: \"tools\", calls: [{ name: \"spawn_subagent\", args: { prompt: \"write a child file\" } }] }\n      : text(\"parent must not get another request\"));\n    const repo = makeRepo();\n    const agent = quiet(new AutonomousAgent(cfg(gw.url, repo, {\n      continuation: { ...DEFAULT_CONTINUATION, maxTotalSteps: 2 },\n    })));\n    const stateManager = (agent as any).stateManager;\n    const recordProgress = stateManager.recordProgress.bind(stateManager);\n    let injected = false;\n    stateManager.recordProgress = (taskId: string, progress: any) => {\n      if (!injected && progress.objective?.execution?.cumulativeSteps === 2) {\n        injected = true;\n        throw new Error(\"simulated objective budget disk failure\");\n      }\n      return recordProgress(taskId, progress);\n    };\n    try {\n      const turn = await agent.runTurn(\"Delegate one write.\");\n      assert.equal(injected, true, \"the child step budget checkpoint was attempted\");\n      assert.equal(turn.execution, \"FAILED\");\n      assert.equal(turn.reason, \"PERSISTENCE_FAILED\");\n      assert.equal(gw.requests.length, 1, \"only the parent request ran; no child inference or parent retry was submitted\");\n      assert.ok(turn.persistence?.failures.some((failure: string) => /simulated objective budget disk failure/.test(failure)));\n    } finally {\n      agent.shutdown();\n      await gw.close();\n      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"a failed durable budget checkpoint prevents the next inference request\", { timeout: 60_000 }, async () => {\n    const gw = await startGateway(() => write(\"must-not-run.txt\"));\n    const repo = makeRepo();\n    const agent = quiet(new AutonomousAgent(cfg(gw.url, repo, {\n      continuation: { ...DEFAULT_CONTINUATION, maxTotalSteps: 2 },\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":44853}},"started_at_ms":1795297848714,"completed_at_ms":1795297848715}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-21T21:50:48.886Z","ordinal":35736,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a20017-2e36-7df2-ba4e-1b609a140000","call_id":"call_c64275d4eeba4d7ca221ab3b8eb03c58","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 7176)\nTotal output lines: 456\n\norigin/main:docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:33:## WP-P10-02 — Durable task-level execution budgets\norigin/main:docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:79:**Priority:** P1 · **Complexity:** M/L · **Dependencies:** WP-P10-02.\norigin/main:docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:108:2. **WP-P10-02** aggregate budgets across direct, delegated, retry and resume paths (P0).\norigin/main:docs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:19:- v1.3 PA-1, PA-2 and PA-3 already cover parallel visibility, verified integration and goal semantics. PA-4 stages this assignment against those units and the active WP-P10-02 durable-budget work.\norigin/main:docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:96:| PA-3 | Goal semantics: a ledger entry active from an earlier process resumes **paused** (opencode `goal.ts` boot id), stall counting by failure fingerprint and not turn count, completion decided only by a verifier receipt, an optional token budget rolling up from sub-operations (reference: Codex goal budget); `/team` leaves experimental only after PA-1 and PA-2 | stale goal resumes paused with a visible reason; a model \"I am done\" does not complete a goal | M | P2 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:97:| PA-4 | **Bounded delegation and workflow commands** (trail 428; [baseline](PA4_BASELINE.md)): extend transient `spawn_subagent` and durable operations with a shared validated delegation contract/outcome, enforce authority intersection and recursive/resource limits, then expose real `/goal`, `/loop`, and `/batch` lifecycles through REPL and TUI/sidecar. Reuse `TeamOrchestrator`, `ConvergenceScheduler`, `OperationStore`, `ResourceRegistry`, specialist profiles, provider recovery, completion evidence, and existing stagnation detectors; do not add a second scheduler or workflow store. `/goal` owns an immutable objective and requirement/evidence ledger; `/loop` is bounded and verifier-driven; `/batch` validates a task graph and maps it into existing work units. Parsing, cancellation, pause/resume, status, recovery, and provider-neutral fixtures are part of each command contract. Spec-format validation may proceed independently; lifecycle and shared-contract work depends on PA-1/PA-2 evidence and WP-P10-02, with `/goal` semantics aligned to PA-3. | prompt-only subagent compatibility; parent/profile/session authority intersection and enforced recursive limits; typed non-success and unknown-effect outcomes; each command has durable state, lifecycle controls, recovery and status through supported interfaces; dependency and workspace conflicts cannot silently complete or overwrite; deterministic verifiers and independent review gate acceptance; standard-contract mock plus existing local/cloud fixtures pass without provider changes | L (staged packages) | P1 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:105:PA-4 is staged: the existing operation-spec validator can be reused independently; command lifecycles and shared delegation changes follow WP-P10-02 and verified PA-1/PA-2 gates. `/goal` must also satisfy PA-3 before promotion.\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport test from \"node:test\";\nimport { dispatchToolCallImpl } from \"../src/core/dispatch_tool_call.js\";\nimport { resolveDelegationContract } from \"../src/core/delegation_contract.js\";\n\ntest(\"delegation contract refuses capabilities outside the inherited intersection\", () => {\n  const contract = {\n    id: \"child-1\",\n    parentId: \"parent-1\",\n    objective: \"Inspect source\",\n    profile: \"semantic_explorer\",\n    inputs: {},\n    authorizedScope: [\"src\"],\n    permittedCapabilities: [\"fs_read\"],\n    executionMode: \"transient\" as const,\n    requiresVerification: false,\n    requiresIndependentReview: false,\n  };\n  const layers = [\"parent\", \"profile\", \"task\", \"session\", \"workspace\"].map((source) => ({\n    source: source as \"parent\" | \"profile\" | \"task\" | \"session\" | \"workspace\",\n    authorizedScope: [\"*\"],\n    permittedCapabilities: [\"fs_read\"],\n  }));\n  assert.deepEqual(resolveDelegationContract(contract, layers).permittedCapabilities, [\"fs_read\"]);\n  assert.throws(() => resolveDelegationContract({ ...contract, permittedCapabilities: [\"fs_write\"] }, layers), /unauthorized capability/);\n});\n\ntest(\"dispatcher denies a delegated tool omitted from its host allowlist\", async () => {\n  const agent: any = {\n    delegatedToolAllowList: new Set([\"read_file\"]),\n    config: { dryRun: false },\n    activeWorktree: undefined,\n    currentTaskId: \"parent-1\",\n    capabilityRegistry: { getByToolName: (name: string) => ({ id: name }) },\n    lastToolReceipts: [],\n    getEffectiveTools: () => [],\n  };\n  const result = await dispatchToolCallImpl.call(agent, {\n    id: \"call-1\",\n    function: { name: \"write_file\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ path: \"src/a.ts\", content: \"bad\" }) },\n  } as any, 1, \"subagent\");\n  assert.equal(result.receipt.status, \"DENIED\");\n  assert.equal(result.receipt.denialReason, \"DELEGATION_AUTHORITY\");\n  assert.equal(result.receipt.candidateMutated, false);\n});\n    try {\n      const port = await new Promise<number>((resolve) => server.listen(0, \"127.0.0.1\", () => resolve((server.address() as any).port)));\n      agent = new AutonomousAgent({ endpoint: `http://127.0.0.1:${port}/v1`, model: \"test\", maxSteps: 2, temperature: 0, workspace: repo, shell: \"bash\", worktree: true, approvalMode: \"auto\", fullAccess: true });\n      await agent.run(\"do not merge an unverified change\");\n      const active = agent.getActiveWorktree();\n      assert.ok(active, \"missing verification retains the speculative worktree\");\n      assert.strictEqual((agent as any).verifiedWorktreeCompletion, false);\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(active!.worktreePath, \"unverified.txt\")), true);\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(repo, \"unverified.txt\")), false);\n      assert.strictEqual(agent.discardActiveWorktree().success, true);\n      // With no applicable verifier, task_completed is accepted as UNVERIFIED (no guessed `npm test` refusal loop),\n      // so the model is not asked for a second turn.\n      assert.strictEqual(requests, 1);\n      const turn = agent.getLastTurnResult();\n      assert.strictEqual(turn?.execution, \"COMPLETED\");\n      assert.strictEqual(turn?.outcome, \"UNVERIFIED\");\n      assert.strictEqual(turn?.reason, \"NO_APPLICABLE_VERIFIER\");\n    } finally {\n      if (agent?.getActiveWorktree()) agent.discardActiveWorktree();\n      agent?.shutdown();\n      server.closeAllConnections();\n      await new Promise<void>((resolve) => server.close(() => resolve()));\n      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"issue 11 worktree subagents cannot mutate the original workspace\", async () => {\n    const repo = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-subagent-authority-\"));\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(repo, \"base.txt\"), \"base\\n\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(repo, \"Makefile\"), \"test:\\n\\t@true\\n\");\n    execSync(\"git init -q && git config user.name 'Nexus Test' && git config user.email 'nexus@example.invalid' && git add . && git commit -qm baseline\", { cwd: repo, stdio: \"ignore\" });\n    const originalWorkspaceWrite = path.join(repo, \"subagent-root-escape.txt\");\n    let streamRequests = 0;\n    let childRequests = 0;\n    const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {\n      if (req.headers[\"x-nexus-purpose\"] === \"capabilities\") { res.setHeader(\"content-type\", \"application/json\"); res.end('{\"data\":[]}'); return; } // capability discovery: no catalog\n      let body = \"\";\n      req.on(\"data\", (chunk) => { body += chunk; });\n      req.on(\"end\", () => {\n        const request = JSON.parse(body || \"{}\");\n        if (request.stream) {\n          streamRequests++;\n          const calls = streamRequests === 1 ? [\n            { index: 0, id: \"write\", type: \"function\", function: { name: \"write_file\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ path: \"parent-worktree.txt\", content: \"parent\\n\" }) } },\n            { index: 1, id: \"spawn\", type: \"function\", function: { name: \"spawn_subagent\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ prompt: \"write to the original checkout\", profile: \"implementer\", max_steps: 3 }) } },\n            { index: 2, id: \"complete\", type: \"function\", function: { name: \"task_completed\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ summary: \"Parent task finished.\" }) } },\n          ] : [];\n          res.writeHead(200, { \"Content-Type\": \"text/event-stream\" });\n          res.end(`data: ${JSON.stringify({ choices: [{ delta: { content: \"Exercise inherited worktree authority.\", tool_calls: calls } }] })}\\n\\ndata: [DONE]\\n\\n`);\n          return;\n        }\n        childRequests++;\n        if (childRequests === 3) {\n          res.writeHead(200, { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" });\n          res.end(JSON.stringify({ choices: [{ message: { role: \"assistant\", content: \"The attempted write escaped the authorized worktree, so I stopped and reported the boundary failure.\" } }] }));\n          return;\n        }\n        const call = childRequests === 1\n          ? { name: \"run_command\", args: { command: \"printf child > child-worktree.txt\" } }\n          : { name: \"run_command\", args: { command: `printf escaped > ${JSON.stringify(originalWorkspaceWrite)}` } };\n        res.writeHead(200, { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" });\n        res.end(JSON.stringify({ choices: [{ message: { role: \"assistant\", tool_calls: [{ id: `child-${childRequests}`, type: \"function\", function: { name: call.name, arguments: JSON.stringify(call.args) } }] } }] }));\n      });\n    });\n    let agent: AutonomousAgent | undefined;\n    try {\n      const port = await new Promise<number>((resolve) => server.listen(0, \"127.0.0.1\", () => resolve((server.address() as any).port)));\n      // The parent spends one task-wide inference step before delegating; leave three for the child sequence.\n      agent = new AutonomousAgent({ endpoint: `http://127.0.0.1:${port}/v1`, model: \"test\", maxSteps: 4, temperature: 0, workspace: repo, shell: \"bash\", worktree: true, approvalMode: \"auto\", fullAccess: true });\n      await agent.run(\"exercise child mutation boundary\");\n      const active = agent.getActiveWorktree();\n      assert.ok(active, \"unverified parent worktree remains recoverable\");\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(originalWorkspaceWrite), false, \"child shell must not mutate the original checkout\");\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(active!.worktreePath, \"parent-worktree.txt\")), true, \"parent mutation remains in its intended worktree\");\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(active!.worktreePath, \"child-worktree.txt\")), true, \"child retains the parent's authorized mutation destination\");\n      assert.strictEqual(streamRequests, 1);\n      assert.strictEqual(childRequests, 3);\n      assert.strictEqual(agent.discardActiveWorktree().success, true);\n    } finally {\n      agent?.shutdown();\n      server.closeAllConnections();\n      await new Promise<void>((resolve) => server.close(() => resolve()));\n      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"worktree-enabled runSubagent refuses to start without inherited worktree authority\", async () => {\n    const repo = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-subagent-no-authority-\"));\n    execSync(\"git init -q\", { cwd: repo, stdio: \"ignore\" });\n    let requests = 0;\n    const server = http.createServer((req, res) => { if (req.headers[\"x-nexus-purpose\"] === \"capabilities\") { res.end('{\"data\":[]}'); return; } requests++; res.writeHead(500).end(); });\n    let agent: AutonomousAgent | undefined;\n    try {\n      const port = await new Promise<number>((resolve) => server.listen(0, \"127.0.0.1\", () => resolve((server.address() as any).port)));\n      agent = new AutonomousAgent({ endpoint: `http://127.0.0.1:${port}/v1`, model: \"test\", maxSteps: 2, temperature: 0, workspace: repo, shell: \"bash\", worktree: true });\n      await assert.rejects(agent.runSubagent(\"must not dispatch without a worktree\"), /without an established worktree authority/);\n      assert.strictEqual(requests, 0, \"refusal happens before inference\");\n      assert.st…1176 tokens truncated…\n\n      // 3. safe command allowed in dry-run\n      const resSafe = await bridge.executeTool(\"run_command\", {\n        command: \"echo 'safe probe'\",\n      });\n      assert.strictEqual(resSafe.success, true);\n      assert.ok(resSafe.output.includes(\"safe probe\"));\n    } finally {\n      bridge.shutdown();\n      fs.rmSync(tmpDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"RustCoreBridge read-only mode blocks file edits and non-safe commands\", async () => {\n    const tmpDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus_readonly_test_\"));\n    const { RustCoreBridge } = await import(\"../src/tools.js\");\n    const bridge = new RustCoreBridge(tmpDir, \"bash\", undefined, false, true);\n    try {\n      const resWrite = await bridge.executeTool(\"write_file\", {\n        path: \"blocked.txt\",\n        content: \"Should fail\",\n      });\n      assert.strictEqual(resWrite.success, false);\n      assert.ok(resWrite.error?.includes(\"Read-only mode violation\"));\n\n      const resCmd = await bridge.executeTool(\"run_command\", {\n        command: \"rm -f something.txt\",\n      });\n      assert.strictEqual(resCmd.success, false);\n      assert.ok(resCmd.error?.includes(\"Read-only mode violation\"));\n\n      const mutatedPaths: string[] = [];\n      for (const [command, target] of [\n        [\"echo payload > echo-redirection.txt\", \"echo-redirection.txt\"],\n        [\"ls .; echo payload > compound-redirection.txt\", \"compound-redirection.txt\"],\n        [\"cat /etc/hosts > cat-redirection.txt\", \"cat-redirection.txt\"],\n        [\"echo payload | tee tee-redirection.txt\", \"tee-redirection.txt\"],\n        [\"git status && echo payload > chained-redirection.txt\", \"chained-redirection.txt\"],\n      ]) {\n        await bridge.executeTool(\"run_command\", { command });\n        if (fs.existsSync(path.join(tmpDir, target))) mutatedPaths.push(target);\n      }\n      assert.deepStrictEqual(mutatedPaths, [], \"read-only shell cannot mutate through redirection or compound syntax\");\n    } finally {\n      bridge.shutdown();\n      fs.rmSync(tmpDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"RustCoreBridge fails closed when an isolated worktree shell loses its sandbox\", async () => {\n    const tmpDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus_required_sandbox_\"));\n    const { RustCoreBridge } = await import(\"../src/tools.js\");\n    const bridge = new RustCoreBridge(tmpDir, \"bash\", undefined, false, false, \"none\", true);\n    try {\n      const result = await bridge.executeTool(\"run_command\", { command: \"echo escaped > fallback-mutation.txt\" });\n      assert.strictEqual(result.success, false);\n      assert.ok(result.error?.includes(\"Worktree isolation violation\"));\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(tmpDir, \"fallback-mutation.txt\")), false);\n    } finally {\n      bridge.shutdown();\n      fs.rmSync(tmpDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"run_tests keeps repository test side effects inside worktree authority and honors read-only, dry-run, and required sandbox\", async () => {\n    const base = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-run-tests-authority-\"));\n    const repo = path.join(base, \"repo\");\n    } finally {\n      unavailableSandbox.shutdown();\n      noSandbox.shutdown();\n      process.env.PATH = oldPath;\n      fs.rmSync(base, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"read-only subagent run_tests cannot mutate the parent worktree, original repository, or outside path\", async () => {\n    const base = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-subagent-run-tests-authority-\"));\n    const repo = path.join(base, \"repo\");\n    fs.mkdirSync(repo);\n    const rootTarget = path.join(repo, \"test-wrote-root.txt\");\n    const outsideTarget = path.join(base, \"test-wrote-outside.txt\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(repo, \"Makefile\"), [\n      \"test:\",\n      `\\t@mkdir -p generated; printf worktree > generated/test-output.txt 2>/dev/null; printf root > ${JSON.stringify(rootTarget)} 2>/dev/null; printf outside > ${JSON.stringify(outsideTarget)} 2>/dev/null; true`,\n      \"\",\n    ].join(\"\\n\"));\n    execSync(\"git init -q && git config user.name 'Nexus Test' && git config user.email 'nexus@example.invalid' && git add . && git commit -qm baseline\", { cwd: repo, stdio: \"ignore\" });\n    let parentRequests = 0;\n    let childRequests = 0;\n    const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {\n      if (req.headers[\"x-nexus-purpose\"] === \"capabilities\") { res.setHeader(\"content-type\", \"application/json\"); res.end('{\"data\":[]}'); return; } // capability discovery: no catalog\n      let body = \"\";\n      req.on(\"data\", (chunk) => { body += chunk; });\n      req.on(\"end\", () => {\n        const request = JSON.parse(body || \"{}\");\n        if (request.stream) {\n          parentRequests++;\n          const calls = parentRequests === 1 ? [\n            { index: 0, id: \"spawn\", type: \"function\", function: { name: \"spawn_subagent\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ prompt: \"run the repository tests\", profile: \"tester\", max_steps: 2 }) } },\n            { index: 1, id: \"complete\", type: \"function\", function: { name: \"task_completed\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ summary: \"Parent finished.\" }) } },\n          ] : [];\n          res.writeHead(200, { \"Content-Type\": \"text/event-stream\" });\n          res.end(`data: ${JSON.stringify({ choices: [{ delta: { content: \"Delegate the test request.\", tool_calls: calls } }] })}\\n\\ndata: [DONE]\\n\\n`);\n          return;\n        }\n        childRequests++;\n        const call = childRequests === 1\n          ? { name: \"run_tests\", args: {} }\n          : { name: \"task_completed\", args: { summary: \"Child finished.\" } };\n        res.writeHead(200, { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" });\n        res.end(JSON.stringify({ choices: [{ message: { role: \"assistant\", tool_calls: [{ id: `child-${childRequests}`, type: \"function\", function: { name: call.name, arguments: JSON.stringify(call.args) } }] } }] }));\n      });\n    });\n    let agent: AutonomousAgent | undefined;\n    try {\n      const port = await new Promise<number>((resolve) => server.listen(0, \"127.0.0.1\", () => resolve((server.address() as any).port)));\n      // The parent spends one step delegating; reserve two child steps for run_tests and its completion report.\n      agent = new AutonomousAgent({ endpoint: `http://127.0.0.1:${port}/v1`, model: \"test\", maxSteps: 3, temperature: 0, workspace: repo, shell: \"bash\", worktree: true, readOnly: true });\n      await agent.run(\"delegate a read-only test request\");\n      const active = agent.getActiveWorktree();\n      assert.strictEqual(childRequests, 2, \"the subagent receives a run_tests tool result and then completes\");\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(active?.worktreePath || \"\", \"generated\", \"test-output.txt\")), false);\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(rootTarget), false, \"the subagent cannot mutate the original checkout\");\n      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(outsideTarget), false, \"the subagent cannot mutate outside the parent boundary\");\n      assert.strictEqual(parentRequests, 1);\n    } finally {\n      if (agent?.getActiveWorktree()) agent.discardActiveWorktree();\n      agent?.shutdown();\n      server.closeAllConnections();\n      await new Promise<void>((resolve) => server.close(() => resolve()));\n      fs.rmSync(base, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"the total step budget is shared by durable resume instead of resetting per invocation\", { timeout: 60_000 }, async () => {\n    const gw = await startGateway((n) => write(`resume-${n}.txt`));\n    const repo = makeRepo();\n    const agent = quiet(new AutonomousAgent(cfg(gw.url, repo, {\n      maxSteps: 30,\n      continuation: { ...DEFAULT_CONTINUATION, maxTotalSteps: 2 },\n    })));\n    try {\n      const first = await agent.runTurn(\"Keep writing distinct files.\");\n      assert.equal(first.reason, \"STEP_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED\");\n      assert.equal(first.steps.used, 2);\n      assert.equal(gw.requests.length, 2);\n\n      const resumed = await agent.runTurn(\"\", undefined, { resume: true });\n      assert.equal(resumed.execution, \"LIMIT_REACHED\");\n      assert.equal(resumed.reason, \"STEP_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED\");\n      assert.equal(gw.requests.length, 2, \"resume at an exhausted budget submits no new inference request\");\n    } finally {\n      agent.shutdown();\n      await gw.close();\n      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"a delegated helper consumes only the parent's remaining durable steps\", { timeout: 60_000 }, async () => {\n    let writes = 0;\n    const gw = await startGateway((_n, body) => {\n      const subagent = (body.messages as any[]).some((message) => typeof message.content === \"string\" && message.content.includes(\"[Subagent Objective]\"));\n      if (!subagent) return { kind: \"tools\", calls: [{ name: \"spawn_subagent\", args: { prompt: \"write until stopped\", profile: \"implementer\" } }] };\n      return write(`shared-${++writes}.txt`);\n    });\n    const repo = makeRepo();\n    const agent = quiet(new AutonomousAgent(cfg(gw.url, repo, {\n      worktree: true,\n      continuation: { ...DEFAULT_CONTINUATION, maxTotalSteps: 3 },\n    })));\n    try {\n      const turn = await agent.runTurn(\"Delegate an open-ended sequence of writes.\");\n      assert.equal(turn.execution, \"LIMIT_REACHED\");\n      assert.equal(turn.reason, \"STEP_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED\");\n      assert.equal(turn.steps.used, 3);\n      assert.equal(agent.getObjective()!.execution!.cumulativeSteps, 3);\n      assert.equal(gw.requests.length, 3, \"one parent request and exactly two delegated requests consumed the budget\");\n      assert.equal(writes, 2);\n      const workspace = agent.getActiveWorktree()?.worktreePath ?? repo;\n      assert.ok(fs.existsSync(path.join(workspace, \"shared-1.txt\")));\n      assert.ok(fs.existsSync(path.join(workspace, \"shared-2.txt\")));\n    } finally {\n      if (agent.getActiveWorktree()) agent.discardActiveWorktree();\n      agent.shutdown();\n      await gw.close();\n      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"a delegated inference is not sent when saving its shared budget fails\", { timeout: 60_000 }, async () => {\n    const gw = await startGateway((n) => n === 1\n      ? { kind: \"tools\", calls: [{ name: \"spawn_subagent\", args: { prompt: \"write a child file\" } }] }\n      : text(\"parent must not get another request\"));\n    const repo = makeRepo();\n    const agent = quiet(new AutonomousAgent(cfg(gw.url, repo, {\n      continuation: { ...DEFAULT_CONTINUATION, maxTotalSteps: 2 },\n    })));\n    const stateManager = (agent as any).stateManager;\n    const recordProgress = stateManager.recordProgress.bind(stateManager);\n    let injected = false;\n    stateManager.recordProgress = (taskId: string, progress: any) => {\n      if (!injected && progress.objective?.execution?.cumulativeSteps === 2) {\n        injected = true;\n        throw new Error(\"simulated objective budget disk failure\");\n      }\n      return recordProgress(taskId, progress);\n    };\n    try {\n      const turn = await agent.runTurn(\"Delegate one write.\");\n      assert.equal(injected, true, \"the child step budget checkpoint was attempted\");\n      assert.equal(turn.execution, \"FAILED\");\n      assert.equal(turn.reason, \"PERSISTENCE_FAILED\");\n      assert.equal(gw.requests.length, 1, \"only the parent request ran; no child inference or parent retry was submitted\");\n      assert.ok(turn.persistence?.failures.some((failure: string) => /simulated objective budget disk failure/.test(failure)));\n    } finally {\n      agent.shutdown();\n      await gw.close();\n      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"a failed durable budget checkpoint prevents the next inference request\", { timeout: 60_000 }, async () => {\n    const gw = await startGateway(() => write(\"must-not-run.txt\"));\n    const repo = makeRepo();\n    const agent = quiet(new AutonomousAgent(cfg(gw.url, repo, {\n      continuation: { ...DEFAULT_CONTINUATION, maxTotalSteps: 2 },\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20014-b98e-7f50-9b44-1c38f2a1201a","create_time":1795297848.886539}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":15947,"sampled_through_sequence":15944,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
